# DustMSHA regression test — Phase 18 MSHA worker exposure tracking.
#
# Physics:
#   PM_resp = dust_pm10 [ug/m3] / 1000           [mg/m3]
#   dose   += PM_resp * dt / 3600                [mg/m3/h]
#   TWA_8h  = dose / 8.0                         [mg/m3]
#   PEL = 5.0 mg/m3 (30 CFR Part 56).
#
# msha_shift_duration_s=1.0 causes shift resets at t=1.0 s (step 2)
# and t=2.0 s (step 4) within the 5-step test.
#
# Two receptors: fence_N at (500,2900) and fence_S at (500,100).
#
# Expected results:
#   (1) [DUST DEBUG] Phase 18 printed each step with TWA_max >= 0.
#   (2) Shift resets logged at steps 2 and 4 (t=1.0 and 2.0 s).
#   (3) msha_exposure.csv: header + 5 rows; TWA_max increases each step.
#   (4) msha_exposure.csv n_cells_exceed = 0 (far below 5 mg/m3).
#   (5) msha_shift_summary.csv: 2 rows (shifts at t=1.0 s and 2.0 s).
#   (6) msha_receptor_fence_N.csv and msha_receptor_fence_S.csv: 5 rows each.
#   (7) plt_dust_00005 contains 18 variables including
#       dust_msha_dose_mg_m3_h, dust_msha_twa_mg_m3,
#       dust_msha_exceed, dust_msha_shift_twa.
#   (8) DustMetadata.json: n_variables=18.
#   (9) Setting msha_pel_mg_m3=1e-15: n_cells_exceed > 0 once PM is present.
#  (10) Run exits code 0.
#
# References:
#   30 CFR Part 56: https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-30/chapter-I/subchapter-K/part-56
#   MSHA dust: https://www.msha.gov/rules-regs/dust
#   Stayner et al. (1998). https://doi.org/10.1164/ajrccm.157.1.9703022
#   Attfield & Morring (1992). https://doi.org/10.1002/ajim.4700220311
#   ERF_FireStatsOutput.H (CSV pattern):
#     https://github.com/hgopalan/ERF/blob/ERF-Fire/Source/Fire/ERF_FireStatsOutput.H

